ise has no test. The verdict is committed as `4f7a4e68` with trailer `WI: WI-881`, in `docs/reviews/wi-881/001-ADJUDICATE-291f389.md`. It ends with `SITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment;first-approval`.\n\n**What holds up:** on Windows the session child now starts suspended inside its own job object, so a deadline kill reaches every process it spawns. A child that can't be contained is killed before it runs. The selected tests in `tests/test_session_stdin.py` pass: 23 passed, inside an outer job, so nesting a job inside a job works.\n\n**Amendment: `VERDICT: MEANING rows=2`, neither blessed:**\n- **LLR-026:** it says a deadline or interruption \"ends the whole session process tree\". On POSIX the code only kills the child's process group. A descendant that leaves that group survives and can keep editing the worktree. That covers one that calls `setsid()`, which daemonizing tools do, or one that runs in its own group. That's ordinary agent behaviour, so it is in scope under §6. I reasoned this from POSIX semantics; I couldn't reproduce it on this Windows box.\n- **TC-026:** it now claims to verify SR-238, but leaves three things unchecked:\n  - the interruption path, which has its own `KeyboardInterrupt` branch;\n  - refusing a Windows child that can't be contained;\n  - SR-238's \"before the coordinator continues\". Neither platform waits for descendants to end, and the test allows the grandchild up to 5 s.\n\n**First approval: `OUTCOME: RETURN rows=1` (SR-238).** The row itself is well made: its trigger, rationale, hat and parent need are all right. But \"every descendant has ended before the coordinator continues\" doesn't hold on POSIX, the timing bound isn't enforced, and interruption has no test.\n\n**Acts:** none. I edited no registry cells and took no snapshot.\n\n**Decision for you:** WI-881's spec is an ordinary one, so intake won't mint follow-ups from it. I wrote two corrective drafts in the verdict file, and the lane needs to answer them before it merges:\n1. Either narrow SR-238 and LLR-026 to processes still in the session's process group (POSIX) or job (Windows), recording the POSIX gap; or strengthen the POSIX mechanism.\n2. Add tests to TC-026 for the interruption path and for refusing a child that can't be contained. Pick one timing bound: either make the coordinator wait for descendants to end, or state the bound in SR-238 and have the test assert it.\n\nThen resubmit SR-238, LLR-026 and TC-026 together.","ttft_ms":2596,"type":"result","duration_ms":143615,"uuid":"0c2891dc-9aab-4d30-80a4-36cccfc3f079","ttft_stream_ms":1164,"time_to_request_ms":220,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":17,"system_prompt":35,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":104,"input_hooks":1,"transcript_persist":1,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":10,"engine_pickup":0,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":13,"message_normalization":14,"client_creation":4,"request_build":12},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":50,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":250,"time_to_request_major_faults":7143,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"changed_files","slowest_producer_ms":85,"cpu_ms":125,"major_faults":3854,"changed_files_reread":7},"first_content_frame_ms":1165,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}]
