{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KuEuPtf8xMYx4WKpHD3mVH","type":"tool_result","content":"291f3892 WI-881: Spine intent: a deadline or interruption ends the session's whole process tree\n19b48f34 WI-881: A Windows session's deadline kill ends its tree through a job object, not taskkill\n?? docs/reviews/wi-881/\n docs/decisions/wi-881.toml                    |  11 ++\n docs/id-watermark                             |   4 +-\n docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml |   8 +-\n docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml    |  14 +++\n docs/test/test-cases.toml                     |   6 +-\n project-trajectory/RESYNC_PACK.md             |  35 +++++++\n project-trajectory/scripts/agent_session.py   | 141 +++++++++++++++++++------\n tests/test_session_stdin.py                   | 145 ++++++++++++++++++++++----\n 8 files changed, 303 insertions(+), 61 deletions(-)\n# docs/decisions/wi-881.toml — WI-881's lane: delegated decisions (coordinator).\n# Format: project-trajectory/decisions.template.toml.\n\nhigh_risk = [\"D-001\"]\n\n[decision.D-001]\ndecided = \"A Windows session's tree kill is a job object, not taskkill: the child is created suspended, assigned to its own job, then resumed with ntdll's NtResumeProcess, and a deadline kill terminates the job. On this workstation taskkill /F [/T] /PID times out after about 61 s and kills nothing (the builder's probes, 2026-10-10), so before this change only proc.kill() worked and a grandchild survived every deadline kill. NtResumeProcess is undocumented but long-standing; it is used because Popen discards the child's primary-thread handle, and the documented route (a thread snapshot to find that thread) takes about 1.2 s here. A child that cannot be contained is killed before it runs and the session errors; there is no fallback to an uncontained child. Probed live through the new spawn: node spawning a child, codex --version and claude --version all ran inside the job.\"\nalternative = \"Resume through the documented thread-snapshot route (OpenThread plus ResumeThread) at about 1.2 s per spawn, or kill the direct child and walk the process list (1.2 s, and it misses a grandchild whose parent has exited).\"\nreversal_cost = \"Low: the resume call is one function (_contain_in_job); swapping it for the documented route changes no interface.\"\nwhy_not_escalated = \"The owner's rule is to fix the single point of failure without a fallback path; the job object does that, and the undocumented call is isolated in one function the full-lane review will judge.\"\nreview = \"\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a511e73-e906-4589-9f31-ae73f8534ed7","uuid":"3f38170e-b157-4f06-855b-52fd71c2ccf6","timestamp":"2026-10-10T16:57:13.482Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"291f3892 WI-881: Spine intent: a deadline or interruption ends the session's whole process tree\n19b48f34 WI-881: A Windows session's deadline kill ends its tree through a job object, not taskkill\n?? docs/reviews/wi-881/\n docs/decisions/wi-881.toml                    |  11 ++\n docs/id-watermark                             |   4 +-\n docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml |   8 +-\n docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml    |  14 +++\n docs/test/test-cases.toml                     |   6 +-\n project-trajectory/RESYNC_PACK.md             |  35 +++++++\n project-trajectory/scripts/agent_session.py   | 141 +++++++++++++++++++------\n tests/test_session_stdin.py                   | 145 ++++++++++++++++++++++----\n 8 files changed, 303 insertions(+), 61 deletions(-)\n# docs/decisions/wi-881.toml — WI-881's lane: delegated decisions (coordinator).\n# Format: project-trajectory/decisions.template.toml.\n\nhigh_risk = [\"D-001\"]\n\n[decision.D-001]\ndecided = \"A Windows session's tree kill is a job object, not taskkill: the child is created suspended, assigned to its own job, then resumed with ntdll's NtResumeProcess, and a deadline kill terminates the job. On this workstation taskkill /F [/T] /PID times out after about 61 s and kills nothing (the builder's probes, 2026-10-10), so before this change only proc.kill() worked and a grandchild survived every deadline kill. NtResumeProcess is undocumented but long-standing; it is used because Popen discards the child's primary-thread handle, and the documented route (a thread snapshot to find that thread) takes about 1.2 s here. A child that cannot be contained is killed before it runs and the session errors; there is no fallback to an uncontained child. Probed live through the new spawn: node spawning a child, codex --version and claude --version all ran inside the job.\"\nalternative = \"Resume through the documented thread-snapshot route (OpenThread plus ResumeThread) at about 1.2 s per spawn, or kill the direct child and walk the process list (1.2 s, and it misses a grandchild whose parent has exited).\"\nreversal_cost = \"Low: the resume call is one function (_contain_in_job); swapping it for the documented route changes no interface.\"\nwhy_not_escalated = \"The owner's rule is to fix the single point of failure without a fallback path; the job object does that, and the undocumented call is isolated in one function the full-lane review will judge.\"\nreview = \"\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
